    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A hallway leads to <var>r</var> rooms via <var>r</var> doors. Given <var>n</var> pairs of room numbers, representing a start room <var>a</var> and a destination room <var>b</var>, labelled from <const>1</const> to <var>r</var> inclusive, find the amount of times each door was opened.<br>Return the result for each door, sorted by room number, separated by spaces.<br><br>All doors are closed at the start and immediately after each use.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The number of doors/rooms <var>r</var><br><strong>Line 2:</strong> Number of room changes <var>n</var><br><strong>Next <var>n</var> Lines:</strong> <const>2</const> space-separated values: the original room number <var>a</var> and the destination room number <var>b</var></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong> <const>1</const> Line:</strong> <var>r</var> space-separated values: the number of times each door was opened, sorted by room number</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">2&le;<var>r</var>&le;100<br>1&le;<var>n</var>&le;100</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">3\n2\n1 2\n2 3</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\